{
    "background_story": "Katelyn was a nurse who worked in a busy hospital, but her true calling was in the palliative care unit. She had a gift for understanding the deepest needs of her patients, often going above and beyond to comfort them in their final days. Katelyn's compassion was not limited to her patients, but also extended to their families, who were often struggling to cope with the impending loss. She would sit with them, listen to their stories, and offer a shoulder to cry on. One patient, an elderly woman named Sarah, had been abandoned by her family. Katelyn took it upon herself to visit Sarah daily, bringing her favorite books and flowers. As Sarah's condition worsened, Katelyn was by her side, holding her hand and whispering words of comfort until the end. Katelyn's selfless compassion inspired her colleagues and earned her the nickname 'Angel of Mercy'.",
